// Helper (not a test): the declarations the cross-file overflow fixtures
// resolve against.
//
// Issue #1303 - ADR-044 makes `clamp` the DEFAULT overflow behavior, but no
// symbol type carried `overflowBehavior`. The fact was authored where the
// declaration was read and had nowhere to live, so it survived only as long as
// codegen was still looking at the declaring file. Cross a file boundary and
// the declared behavior was gone: codegen emitted plain C arithmetic.
//
// Each declaration below is 250, five short of UINT8_MAX, so a `+ 10` either
// saturates to 255 (clamp) or wraps to 4 (wrap). The two are never equal, so
// the consuming fixture can tell them apart at runtime.

u8 defaultedCounter <- 250;
clamp u8 explicitClampCounter <- 250;
wrap u8 explicitWrapCounter <- 250;

scope Counter {
    public u8 value <- 250;
    public wrap u8 wrappingValue <- 250;
}
